  "functions": [
    "FUNC.SYD"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "SYD admits negative cost and fractional periods, forms (life + 1) - per in x87, and flushes subnormal denominators",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, SYD(cost, salvage, life, per) admits negative cost and fractional per/life while rejecting salvage < 0, life <= 0, per <= 0, or per > life (by >= DBL_MIN) with #NUM!. It evaluates denominator = life * (life + 1) / 2 in x87 (flushing nonfinite or subnormal denominators to 0 and returning #DIV/0!), stores basis = cost - salvage (flushed if subnormal), and returns ((basis * ((life + 1) - per)) / denominator) with every operation stored from x87 PC64. All 1,207 full-bank SYD rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20430 (1,207/1,207 full-bank and 120/120 pinned SYD rows) and 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 389).",
